{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1019464-haitian-voodoo","id":1019464,"title":"Haitian Voodoo","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-19T15:52:42-08:00","id":1019464,"title":"Haitian Voodoo","content":"Decided to make a separate thread on this<br /> <br /> <br /> Are there any spiritual rotes that denote particular curses I could inflict upon someone as a shaman? If not, what spheres could I use to inflict curses upon someone (like curse them to sickness, to death, to a skin-eating bacteria, to bone deteroriation, etc)<br /> <br /> Also, my char is a Haitian voodooist dreamspeaker. What spheres would I need to be able to do voodoo? Examples being evoking dark forces, using a doll to inflict pain upon someone from afar, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T16:31:12-08:00","id":1019479,"title":"","content":"I sorry bud but either you are just trolling for all your game info or you have never read a Mage book. <br /> <br /> If you are new to the game and your ST hasn't let you read over any of the books for whatever reason you should get a new group.<br /> <br /> As far as your questions, from the answers you have gotten on your other threads I would think you should be able to come up with a pretty good idea of what spheres are necessary at the very least. Even if the levels elude you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T16:38:11-08:00","id":1019485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tuch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1019464-haitian-voodoo?p=1019479#post1019479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I sorry bud but either you are just trolling for all your game info or you have never read a Mage book.<br /> <br /> If you are new to the game and your ST hasn't let you read over any of the books for whatever reason you should get a new group.<br /> <br /> As far as your questions, from the answers you have gotten on your other threads I would think you should be able to come up with a pretty good idea of what spheres are necessary at the very least. Even if the levels elude you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Trolling? Are you kidding me? The mechanics of this game confuse me, and oftentimes I am directed to these forums. I'm not trolling and I have read the books, I just need a little extra help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T17:18:00-08:00","id":1019503,"title":"","content":"I see the question as legitimate for an inexperience Mage player, not everyone has 20 years of experience with the game. Voodoo is the religion, Hoodoo is the magical practice, so it is more of how to use Spheres to practice Hoodoo. Hoodoo would primarily be a mixture of Spirit and Entropy, Spirit to contact the spirit world and Entropy to manipulate probability to bless or to curse. In addition, Life would be good for healing, Correspondence would be good for connecting an individual to a prop like a 'Voodoo' doll and Time would be good for delaying the effects or making the effects conditional.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T17:42:55-08:00","id":1019520,"title":"","content":"This is a legit question. Translating paradigm into spheres chains can be a mental challenge all onto itself.<br /> <br /> Entropy 4 is needed for any kind of life cursing. Arguably you'd need a little bit of Life if you want to specify which pieces of body you harm, but for general things like disease, pain, or deteriation, Entropy 4 will suffice.<br /> <br /> If you want to do any of this from affar, you'll need at least Correspondence 4. Depending on the ST, though, you may be able to use Spirit to get around the Corr requirement by having the spell act on the spirit who then takes it to the cursed one. <br /> <br /> If this is allowed, the. you could instead use a mixture of Spirit and Entropy to curse a guy with Banes that cause disease, epiphlings of pain, or any over appropriate spirits from voodoo. Entropy 4 Spirit 4 would be needed to force the spirit's fate to be tied to the subject's health. Though an easier way to do this would be to simply negotiate with the spirit using Spirit 2.<br /> <br /> It may be possible to make a voodoo doll as a wonder, requiring Prime along with Life, Corr, or Spirit to do so, or as a fetish, requiring only spirit.<br /> <br /> Hope that gives you a starting point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T21:03:25-08:00","id":1019594,"title":"","content":"Let me try my crash course:<br /> <br /> Magic have three main elements: HOW you do. WHAT you do. What you ROLL.<br /> <br /> What you Roll is, in the end, Arete. No mystery. Just that.<br /> <br /> HOW you do, is your PARADIGM. It is yours. You describe how you make your magic. You chant? You bleed? You use The Force? Psychic powers? Touch people? Sacrifice wooden dolls? You have to define to some degree what kind of magic you do, in your case, Voodoo. You can create any kind of description in this game. So you don't need a trait to use dolls, you don't need traits to chant, you don't need traits to describe how you do your stuff.<br /> <br /> WHAT you do is SPHERE. The trick is to think on the end of the line. That seems to be where you're struggling with it. Final effect. What your magic do when all is said and done. Spheres don't cover the style of your stuff, only what you make at the end. You turn a plant into an animal? Life. You affect people beyond sight? Correspondence. You calls forth an actual spirit? Spirit. You transfer the sentience of a person to an animal? Mind. And so on. And so forth. Just remember: end.<br /> <br /> Rotes: they're just examples of effects. You don't need them, and they don't substitute Spheres. They are just magic you do regularly and got practiced with. Sometimes it help to go for Rotes first and get their requisites, so you have the examples before you understand the system. If you want so badly to understand the system first, though, forget about them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T01:24:53-08:00","id":1026395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1019464-haitian-voodoo?p=1019520#post1019520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a legit question. Translating paradigm into spheres chains can be a mental challenge all onto itself.<br /> <br /> Entropy 4 is needed for any kind of life cursing. Arguably you'd need a little bit of Life if you want to specify which pieces of body you harm, but for general things like disease, pain, or deteriation, Entropy 4 will suffice.<br /> <br /> If you want to do any of this from affar, you'll need at least Correspondence 4. Depending on the ST, though, you may be able to use Spirit to get around the Corr requirement by having the spell act on the spirit who then takes it to the cursed one.<br /> <br /> If this is allowed, the. you could instead use a mixture of Spirit and Entropy to curse a guy with Banes that cause disease, epiphlings of pain, or any over appropriate spirits from voodoo. Entropy 4 Spirit 4 would be needed to force the spirit's fate to be tied to the subject's health. Though an easier way to do this would be to simply negotiate with the spirit using Spirit 2.<br /> <br /> It may be possible to make a voodoo doll as a wonder, requiring Prime along with Life, Corr, or Spirit to do so, or as a fetish, requiring only spirit.<br /> <br /> Hope that gives you a starting point.</div> </div> </div> </div>How would you suggest a voodoo doll as a fetish could work? Perhaps have a spirit of chaos or something bound to it, and then use it to inflict agg damage on someone or what? Any ideas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T03:15:21-08:00","id":1026430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingJohn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1019464-haitian-voodoo?p=1026395#post1026395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How would you suggest a voodoo doll as a fetish could work? Perhaps have a spirit of chaos or something bound to it, and then use it to inflict agg damage on someone or what? Any ideas?</div> </div> </div> </div>There are a number of spirits that could work. Spirit of Chaos (aka Wyld Spirits) would be rather difficult to negotiate with, and may lead to inconsistent results.<br /> You could use Spirits of Pain, spirits of Revenge, spirits of War... As long as the spirits itself either likes dealing in pain, or at least isn't outright against pain, you can have whichever spirit you want.<br /> <br /> If you want WoD canon spirits, then I'd recommend skimming through Axis Mundi to see which kind of spirit would be most suitable.<br /> If you'd rather stick with the Hatian mythology. Then do a bit of research on their beliefs and see what kinds of spirits they would employ for such a job.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}